course: dictionary
lesson: 14322
title: Strong words, strong feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words are very strong. «Obscene» is one of them. It describes something so rude, shocking or unfair that people feel strongly about it, so the word also tells you how the writer feels.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The school rules say obscene words are not allowed in the playground.» Rules like this keep people safe and respectful, so obscene must mean very rude and not acceptable. Check by swapping in a milder word: "not allowed" fits rude words, but it does not fit "nice" words.
explain: Obscene can also mean shockingly unfair or too much. «The boss made an obscene amount of money while the workers were paid almost nothing.» Money is not rude here. The clue is "the workers were paid almost nothing", which shows the amount is unfair. The writer disapproves.
explain: If you meet something obscene online or in a book, do not share it. Tell a trusted adult, and check a dictionary when you are unsure what a word means.
fact: Obscene means very rude and shocking, often about sex or the body, and not acceptable in public.
fact: Obscene also means shockingly unfair or far too much, as in «an obscene amount of money».
fact: In news reports, «obscene profits» or «obscene waste» shows that the writer strongly disapproves.
fact: Obscene pictures and words are not allowed in school, and you should tell an adult if you see them.
fact: Strong words often show the writer's feelings, so ask yourself whether the writer is shocked, angry or disapproving.
exercise: «The school rules say obscene words are not allowed in the playground.» What does obscene mean here? | Very kind and helpful | *Very rude and shocking, and not acceptable | Very old and worn | Very quiet and gentle
exercise: «The boss made an obscene amount of money.» Which phrase is closest in meaning to obscene here? | A small, sensible amount | Just the right amount for a party | An amount that is hard to count | *Far too much and shockingly unfair
exercise: «The boss made an obscene amount of money while the workers were paid almost nothing.» Which words show the amount is unfair? | *The workers were paid almost nothing | The boss made an | Money while | An amount of
test: Ella sees an obscene picture on a website. What should she do? | Save it to show her brother | *Tell a trusted adult | Forward it to everyone in her class | Share it with her friends to laugh
test: What does obscene mean? | *Very rude and shocking, or far too much and unfair | Very tiny and thin | Very quiet and calm | Very happy and bright
exam: «The waste of food in the canteen was obscene.» What does this tell you about the writer? | The canteen food was delicious | The writer is pleased with the food | *The writer strongly disapproves and thinks it is shockingly wrong | The food was served cold
